## Q4. Does delivery performance relate to customer review scores?

### SQL Query

```sql
SELECT
    CASE
        WHEN o.order_delivered_customer_date >
             o.order_estimated_delivery_date
        THEN 'Late'
        ELSE 'On-time'
    END AS delivery_status,

    COUNT(*) AS orders,

    ROUND(AVG(r.review_score), 2) AS avg_review_score

FROM raw_orders o

JOIN raw_order_reviews r
    ON o.order_id = r.order_id

WHERE o.order_status = 'delivered'
  AND o.order_delivered_customer_date IS NOT NULL
  AND o.order_estimated_delivery_date IS NOT NULL

GROUP BY delivery_status;
```

### Result

| Delivery Status | Orders | Avg Review Score |
| --------------- | -----: | ---------------: |
| On-time         | 88,653 |         **4.29** |
| Late            |  7,700 |         **2.57** |

### Finding

Late deliveries are strongly associated with lower customer satisfaction. On-time orders received an average rating of **4.29**, compared with only **2.57** for late orders — a difference of **1.72 rating points**.

